WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.700 --> 00:00:02.709
Iʿrāb in the Qur'an. Ten verses.

2
00:00:03.159 --> 00:00:07.039
These are real verses. Each one
has a past verb and a naṣb noun.

3
00:00:07.139 --> 00:00:09.856
They also use the rafʿ and
jarr rules we already know.

4
00:00:09.956 --> 00:00:11.694
Same colours. Same method.

5
00:00:12.244 --> 00:00:15.093
Chapter one. Three small
notes for these verses.

6
00:00:15.443 --> 00:00:17.940
First note. Attached pronouns are fixed.

7
00:00:18.190 --> 00:00:22.069
His, her and your can be short endings.
They join the noun before them.

8
00:00:22.169 --> 00:00:23.280
They are the owner.

9
00:00:23.380 --> 00:00:27.271
We split them off, so you can see
the noun's ending. Take his Lord.

10
00:00:27.521 --> 00:00:28.380
‫رَبَّهُ‬

11
00:00:28.730 --> 00:00:30.550
His is the small piece at the end.

12
00:00:31.000 --> 00:00:33.723
Second note. A past
verb can hide its doer.

13
00:00:33.973 --> 00:00:38.986
An order verb hides the word you. In the
same way, a past verb can hide the word he.

14
00:00:39.086 --> 00:00:39.907
‫(هُوَ)‬

15
00:00:40.157 --> 00:00:41.781
It can also hide the word she.

16
00:00:41.881 --> 00:00:42.562
‫(هِيَ)‬

17
00:00:42.912 --> 00:00:44.446
This verb means she tore.

18
00:00:44.546 --> 00:00:45.403
‫قَدَّتْ‬

19
00:00:45.753 --> 00:00:48.239
The ending of this verb
tells us the doer is she.

20
00:00:48.689 --> 00:00:51.298
Third note. Some names never take tanween.

21
00:00:51.548 --> 00:00:52.384
‫آدَمُ‬

22
00:00:52.634 --> 00:00:53.769
‫سُلَيْمَانُ‬

23
00:00:54.019 --> 00:00:55.103
‫دَاوُودَ‬

24
00:00:55.453 --> 00:00:57.118
One damma or one fatha only.

25
00:00:57.368 --> 00:00:59.385
But names like Nuh do take tanween.

26
00:00:59.485 --> 00:01:00.488
‫نُوحٌ‬

27
00:01:01.038 --> 00:01:05.942
Also. Some past verbs end in a letter with
sukūn, like the verb in the second note.

28
00:01:06.042 --> 00:01:10.203
Before al, that last letter takes a
small kasra, just like an order verb.

29
00:01:10.303 --> 00:01:11.578
She closed the doors.

30
00:01:11.828 --> 00:01:13.903
‫غَلَّقَتِ الأَبْوَابَ‬

31
00:01:14.253 --> 00:01:15.499
It is still fixed.

32
00:01:17.733 --> 00:01:19.383
Chapter two. The colour key.

33
00:01:19.633 --> 00:01:22.815
Navy is the verb. Past
and order verbs are fixed.

34
00:01:22.915 --> 00:01:26.425
Orange is the doer. Who did
the action? It takes rafʿ.

35
00:01:26.675 --> 00:01:28.586
The next four jobs all take naṣb.

36
00:01:28.686 --> 00:01:30.606
Pink is the object. What? Whom?

37
00:01:30.706 --> 00:01:32.351
Teal is the purpose. Why?

38
00:01:32.451 --> 00:01:36.358
Brown is time or place. When?
Where? With no preposition.

39
00:01:36.458 --> 00:01:37.957
Olive is the state. How?

40
00:01:38.207 --> 00:01:43.640
The small boxes from last lesson still
work. After a preposition. Ownership.

41
00:01:43.640 --> 00:01:45.356
Adjective. And after wa.

42
00:01:45.906 --> 00:01:47.642
Chapter three. The ten verses.

43
00:01:47.892 --> 00:01:52.109
Read each verse aloud with your
teacher first. Then solve the cards.

44
00:01:52.109 --> 00:01:53.597
Every ending is missing.

45
00:01:54.047 --> 00:01:58.662
Each row is one verse. Next to it are
its reference and the jobs inside it.

46
00:01:58.912 --> 00:02:01.456
Most of them are a short
piece of a longer verse.

47
00:02:01.706 --> 00:02:04.414
On screen, they are written
in our usual spelling.

48
00:02:04.664 --> 00:02:07.565
The naṣb noun is an
object, a time, or a state.

49
00:02:07.815 --> 00:02:11.997
For each verse, we first hear its
meaning. Then we hear it recited.

50
00:02:12.097 --> 00:02:14.836
After that, we box it
together, piece by piece.

51
00:02:17.200 --> 00:02:21.205
Verse one. From Surah Ta-Ha.
And Adam disobeyed his Lord.

52
00:02:21.455 --> 00:02:25.425
‫وَعَصَى آدَمُ رَبَّهُ‬

53
00:02:26.075 --> 00:02:30.259
First, the verb. Disobeyed. It
is a past verb, so it is fixed.

54
00:02:30.359 --> 00:02:34.237
The wa before it means and. It
is a particle. It never changes.

55
00:02:34.337 --> 00:02:35.319
Who disobeyed?

56
00:02:35.669 --> 00:02:36.505
‫آدَمُ‬

57
00:02:36.755 --> 00:02:39.858
Adam. He is the doer, so
he takes rafʿ, with damma.

58
00:02:39.958 --> 00:02:43.436
Only one damma, no tanween.
Some names never take tanween.

59
00:02:43.686 --> 00:02:44.840
Whom did he disobey?

60
00:02:45.290 --> 00:02:46.149
‫رَبَّهُ‬

61
00:02:46.399 --> 00:02:50.837
His Lord. That is the object, so
it takes naṣb. Its sign is fatha.

62
00:02:50.937 --> 00:02:56.030
His is an attached pronoun at the end of
the word. It is the owner, and it is fixed.

63
00:02:56.130 --> 00:02:59.726
Because Lord is owned, it has
no tanween. Just one fatha.

64
00:02:59.976 --> 00:03:01.413
Listen to the verse once more.

65
00:03:01.513 --> 00:03:05.483
‫وَعَصَى آدَمُ رَبَّهُ‬

66
00:03:06.233 --> 00:03:10.154
Verse two. From Surah Hud.
And Nuh called out to his son.

67
00:03:10.404 --> 00:03:13.954
‫وَنَادَى نُوحٌ ابْنَهُ‬

68
00:03:14.604 --> 00:03:18.885
First, the verb. Called out. It
is a past verb, so it is fixed.

69
00:03:18.985 --> 00:03:21.694
The wa before it is a
particle. It never changes.

70
00:03:21.844 --> 00:03:22.693
Who called out?

71
00:03:23.043 --> 00:03:24.046
‫نُوحٌ‬

72
00:03:24.296 --> 00:03:27.257
Nuh. He is the doer, so
he takes rafʿ, with damma.

73
00:03:27.357 --> 00:03:30.072
This name does take
tanween. Damma with tanween.

74
00:03:30.322 --> 00:03:31.268
Whom did he call?

75
00:03:31.718 --> 00:03:32.594
‫ابْنَهُ‬

76
00:03:32.844 --> 00:03:38.113
His son. In English we say called out to
his son. The Arabic has no extra word.

77
00:03:38.213 --> 00:03:41.741
So it is the object. It takes
naṣb. Its sign is fatha.

78
00:03:41.841 --> 00:03:45.665
His is the attached pronoun. It
is the owner, and it is fixed.

79
00:03:45.765 --> 00:03:48.562
Son is owned, so no
tanween. Just one fatha.

80
00:03:49.012 --> 00:03:53.625
Verse three. From Surah An-Naml.
And Sulayman inherited from Dawud.

81
00:03:53.875 --> 00:03:57.477
‫وَوَرِثَ سُلَيْمَانُ دَاوُودَ‬

82
00:03:58.127 --> 00:04:02.520
First, the verb. Inherited. It
is a past verb, so it is fixed.

83
00:04:02.620 --> 00:04:05.329
The wa before it is a
particle. It never changes.

84
00:04:05.479 --> 00:04:06.381
Who inherited?

85
00:04:06.731 --> 00:04:07.866
‫سُلَيْمَانُ‬

86
00:04:08.116 --> 00:04:11.367
Sulayman. He is the doer, so
he takes rafʿ, with damma.

87
00:04:11.467 --> 00:04:14.220
Only one damma. This
name never takes tanween.

88
00:04:14.470 --> 00:04:15.895
Whom did he inherit from?

89
00:04:16.345 --> 00:04:17.429
‫دَاوُودَ‬

90
00:04:17.679 --> 00:04:22.002
Dawud. In English we say from
Dawud. The Arabic has no extra word.

91
00:04:22.102 --> 00:04:24.814
He is the object, so he
takes naṣb, with fatha.

92
00:04:24.914 --> 00:04:28.254
Only one fatha. Like Adam,
this name never takes tanween.

93
00:04:30.400 --> 00:04:34.245
Verse four. From Surah Yusuf.
And she closed the doors.

94
00:04:34.495 --> 00:04:37.925
‫وَغَلَّقَتِ الأَبْوَابَ‬

95
00:04:38.575 --> 00:04:42.426
First, the verb. Closed. It is
a past verb, so it is fixed.

96
00:04:42.526 --> 00:04:45.235
The wa before it is a
particle. It never changes.

97
00:04:45.385 --> 00:04:49.814
Remember the Also box. Before al,
this verb ends in a small kasra.

98
00:04:50.064 --> 00:04:51.461
‫وَغَلَّقَتِ‬

99
00:04:51.811 --> 00:04:53.096
Who closed the doors?

100
00:04:53.446 --> 00:04:56.921
The doer is hidden. The ending
of the verb tells us it is she.

101
00:04:57.021 --> 00:04:57.702
‫(هِيَ)‬

102
00:04:58.052 --> 00:04:59.205
What did she close?

103
00:04:59.655 --> 00:05:01.060
‫الأَبْوَابَ‬

104
00:05:01.310 --> 00:05:05.533
The doors. That is the object, so
it takes naṣb. Its sign is fatha.

105
00:05:05.633 --> 00:05:07.578
It has al, so there is no tanween.

106
00:05:07.928 --> 00:05:12.500
Verse five. From Surah Yusuf. And
she tore his shirt from the back.

107
00:05:12.750 --> 00:05:17.640
‫وَقَدَّتْ قَمِيصَهُ مِنْ دُبُرٍ‬

108
00:05:18.290 --> 00:05:21.015
The verb, tore, is a
past verb. It is fixed.

109
00:05:21.115 --> 00:05:23.824
The wa before it is a
particle. It never changes.

110
00:05:23.974 --> 00:05:24.987
Who tore the shirt?

111
00:05:25.337 --> 00:05:27.547
Again, the doer is hidden. It is she.

112
00:05:27.647 --> 00:05:28.328
‫(هِيَ)‬

113
00:05:28.678 --> 00:05:29.819
What did she tear?

114
00:05:30.269 --> 00:05:31.625
‫قَمِيصَهُ‬

115
00:05:31.875 --> 00:05:35.481
His shirt. That is the object,
so it takes naṣb, with fatha.

116
00:05:35.581 --> 00:05:38.418
His is the owner. Attached
pronouns are fixed.

117
00:05:38.518 --> 00:05:40.561
Shirt is owned, so it has no tanween.

118
00:05:40.811 --> 00:05:43.060
Next comes from. It is a particle.

119
00:05:43.160 --> 00:05:43.998
‫دُبُرٍ‬

120
00:05:44.248 --> 00:05:49.050
The back. It comes after a preposition,
so it takes jarr. Kasra with tanween.

121
00:05:49.400 --> 00:05:54.047
Verse six. From Surah Al-Baqarah.
And He sent down water from the sky.

122
00:05:54.297 --> 00:06:00.997
‫وَأَنْزَلَ مِنَ السَّمَاءِ مَاءً‬

123
00:06:01.647 --> 00:06:04.673
The verb, sent down, is
a past verb. It is fixed.

124
00:06:04.773 --> 00:06:07.482
The wa before it is a
particle. It never changes.

125
00:06:07.632 --> 00:06:08.938
Who sent down the water?

126
00:06:09.288 --> 00:06:11.124
The doer is hidden. It is He.

127
00:06:11.224 --> 00:06:12.045
‫(هُوَ)‬

128
00:06:12.395 --> 00:06:14.644
Next comes from. It is a particle.

129
00:06:14.744 --> 00:06:15.976
‫السَّمَاءِ‬

130
00:06:16.226 --> 00:06:20.174
The sky. After a preposition,
so it takes jarr, with kasra.

131
00:06:20.174 --> 00:06:21.847
It has al, so no tanween.

132
00:06:21.947 --> 00:06:23.211
What did He send down?

133
00:06:23.661 --> 00:06:24.478
‫مَاءً‬

134
00:06:24.728 --> 00:06:27.452
Water. That is the
object, so it takes naṣb.

135
00:06:27.552 --> 00:06:31.060
Water has no al and no owner,
so it takes fatha with tanween.

136
00:06:33.100 --> 00:06:38.265
Verse seven. From Surah Al-Isra. It
means: who took His servant by night.

137
00:06:38.515 --> 00:06:42.015
‫أَسْرَى بِعَبْدِهِ لَيْلًا‬

138
00:06:42.665 --> 00:06:46.498
First, the verb. Took. It is
a past verb, so it is fixed.

139
00:06:46.598 --> 00:06:47.584
Who is the doer?

140
00:06:47.934 --> 00:06:49.770
The doer is hidden. It is He.

141
00:06:49.870 --> 00:06:50.691
‫(هُوَ)‬

142
00:06:51.041 --> 00:06:55.287
The next word starts with a preposition.
The preposition is a particle.

143
00:06:55.387 --> 00:06:56.605
‫بِعَبْدِهِ‬

144
00:06:56.855 --> 00:06:59.364
In English, His servant
looks like an object.

145
00:06:59.464 --> 00:07:04.140
In Arabic, servant comes after a
preposition, so it takes jarr, with kasra.

146
00:07:04.140 --> 00:07:05.823
It is owned, so no tanween.

147
00:07:05.923 --> 00:07:08.760
His is the owner. Attached
pronouns are fixed.

148
00:07:08.860 --> 00:07:09.994
When did He take him?

149
00:07:10.444 --> 00:07:11.265
‫لَيْلًا‬

150
00:07:11.515 --> 00:07:14.430
By night. In Arabic there
is no preposition here.

151
00:07:14.530 --> 00:07:17.991
So it is a time, and it takes
naṣb. Fatha with tanween.

152
00:07:18.341 --> 00:07:23.568
Verse eight. From Surah Al-Fajr. And your
Lord came, and the angels, row after row.

153
00:07:23.818 --> 00:07:32.302
‫وَجَاءَ رَبُّكَ وَالمَلَكُ صَفًّا صَفًّا‬

154
00:07:32.952 --> 00:07:35.691
The verb, came, is a
past verb. It is fixed.

155
00:07:35.791 --> 00:07:38.500
The wa before it is a
particle. It never changes.

156
00:07:38.650 --> 00:07:39.528
Who came?

157
00:07:39.878 --> 00:07:40.749
‫رَبُّكَ‬

158
00:07:40.999 --> 00:07:44.368
Your Lord. That is the doer,
so it takes rafʿ, with damma.

159
00:07:44.468 --> 00:07:47.271
Your is the owner. Attached
pronouns are fixed.

160
00:07:47.371 --> 00:07:49.576
So Lord is owned, and has no tanween.

161
00:07:49.676 --> 00:07:50.707
‫وَالمَلَكُ‬

162
00:07:50.957 --> 00:07:54.900
And the angels. This comes after
wa, so it copies the damma of Lord.

163
00:07:55.150 --> 00:07:56.500
How did the angels come?

164
00:07:56.950 --> 00:07:57.868
‫صَفًّا‬

165
00:07:58.118 --> 00:08:02.768
Row after row. That is the state, so
it takes naṣb. Fatha with tanween.

166
00:08:02.868 --> 00:08:05.911
The word comes twice. Both
times, fatha with tanween.

167
00:08:08.067 --> 00:08:10.089
Verse nine. From Surah Al-Qasas.

168
00:08:10.089 --> 00:08:14.069
And he entered the city at a time
when its people were unaware.

169
00:08:14.319 --> 00:08:20.459
‫وَدَخَلَ المَدِينَةَ عَلَى‬
‫حِينِ غَفْلَةٍ مِنْ أَهْلِهَا‬

170
00:08:21.109 --> 00:08:24.081
The verb, entered, is a
past verb. It is fixed.

171
00:08:24.181 --> 00:08:26.890
The wa before it is a
particle. It never changes.

172
00:08:27.040 --> 00:08:27.948
Who entered?

173
00:08:28.298 --> 00:08:30.134
The doer is hidden. It is he.

174
00:08:30.234 --> 00:08:31.055
‫(هُوَ)‬

175
00:08:31.405 --> 00:08:32.379
What did he enter?

176
00:08:32.829 --> 00:08:34.045
‫المَدِينَةَ‬

177
00:08:34.295 --> 00:08:37.893
The city. That is the object,
so it takes naṣb, with fatha.

178
00:08:38.143 --> 00:08:42.734
Then a group that starts with a
preposition. The preposition is a particle.

179
00:08:42.834 --> 00:08:43.793
‫حِينِ‬

180
00:08:44.043 --> 00:08:48.848
A time. After a preposition, so jarr,
with kasra. Owned, so no tanween.

181
00:08:48.948 --> 00:08:49.818
‫غَفْلَةٍ‬

182
00:08:50.068 --> 00:08:54.395
A time of unawareness. Unawareness
is the owner of a time, so jarr.

183
00:08:54.395 --> 00:08:55.622
Kasra with tanween.

184
00:08:55.722 --> 00:08:58.414
Then another preposition.
It is a particle.

185
00:08:58.514 --> 00:08:59.514
‫أَهْلِهَا‬

186
00:08:59.764 --> 00:09:04.857
Its people. After a preposition, so
jarr, with kasra. Owned, so no tanween.

187
00:09:04.957 --> 00:09:07.790
Its is the owner. Attached
pronouns are fixed.

188
00:09:08.240 --> 00:09:12.857
Verse ten. From Surah An-Naml. So
he smiled, laughing at her words.

189
00:09:13.107 --> 00:09:18.111
‫فَتَبَسَّمَ ضَاحِكًا مِنْ قَوْلِهَا‬

190
00:09:18.761 --> 00:09:21.583
The verb, smiled, is a
past verb. It is fixed.

191
00:09:21.683 --> 00:09:24.818
The small word before it
means so. It is a particle.

192
00:09:24.918 --> 00:09:25.826
Who smiled?

193
00:09:26.176 --> 00:09:27.734
Again, the doer is hidden.

194
00:09:27.834 --> 00:09:28.655
‫(هُوَ)‬

195
00:09:29.005 --> 00:09:30.054
How did he smile?

196
00:09:30.504 --> 00:09:31.445
‫ضَاحِكًا‬

197
00:09:31.695 --> 00:09:33.986
Laughing. Here it is a noun, not a verb.

198
00:09:34.086 --> 00:09:37.454
It is the state, so it takes
naṣb. Fatha with tanween.

199
00:09:37.704 --> 00:09:42.295
Then a group that starts with a
preposition. The preposition is a particle.

200
00:09:42.395 --> 00:09:43.337
‫قَوْلِهَا‬

201
00:09:43.587 --> 00:09:48.545
Her words. After a preposition, so
jarr, with kasra. Owned, so no tanween.

202
00:09:48.645 --> 00:09:51.496
Her is the owner. Attached
pronouns are fixed.

203
00:09:52.146 --> 00:09:54.800
Now it is your turn. Open the Verses tab.

204
00:09:54.900 --> 00:09:56.406
Every ending is missing.

205
00:09:56.506 --> 00:10:00.401
Draw the big boxes first. Verb
and doer, then every other job.

206
00:10:00.501 --> 00:10:02.084
If the doer is hidden, write it.

207
00:10:02.184 --> 00:10:05.198
Then, for every piece, circle
its ending and its job.

208
00:10:05.298 --> 00:10:07.488
If a piece is fixed, circle the dash.

209
00:10:07.588 --> 00:10:10.159
When you finish, check your
work with the answer key.
